{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789290379,"nonce":"QdyuyeqbJ3bJGpEHbfsDGcL9iWA=","message":"Owner's direction (2026-09-13): ash turns off the optimisers that could\nhide a published class, and static linking keeps the symbols. Checked\nagainst ash's source, the precise version is:\n\n- ash's interpreter keeps every function and the whole type table, so a\n  hosted interpreted or Cranelift-tier program needs nothing.\n- ash's AIR passes and its AOT shard sweep both skip what\n  reachable::analyze calls dead, seeded from the entrypoint. A published\n  class the Haxe program never references is dead to them: its AIR is\n  never optimised (harmless) and, under AOT, no body is emitted for it.\n  Static linking preserves emitted symbols but cannot restore an unemitted\n  body, so the seeds must include the published set. Filed on ash as a\n  seam entry: reach_roots supplied by the host, default empty.\n- Once seeded, a static link keeps the bodies and the linked-spoke stubs\n  bind to them directly, which is the 0683393 plan.","files":null}]}